DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kklldduunnllooaadd() system call unloads a kld file from the kernel that was
     previously linked via kldload(2).

     The kklldduunnllooaaddff() system call accepts an additional flags argument, which
     may be one of LINKER_UNLOAD_NORMAL, giving the same behavior as
     kklldduunnllooaadd(), or LINKER_UNLOAD_FORCE, which causes the unload to ignore a
     failure to quiesce the module.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Upon successful completion, the value 0 is returned; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The file referred to by _f_i_l_e_i_d is unloaded unless:

     [EPERM]            You do not have access to unlink the file from the
                        kernel.

     [ENOENT]           The file was not found.

     [EBUSY]            You attempted to unload a file linked by the kernel.

     [EINVAL]           The kklldduunnllooaaddff() system call was passed invalid flags.

